        }
      ],
      "extract": "Let $(W, S), S = \\{s_1, \\dots, s_n\\},$ be a Coxeter system. Thus, $W$ is a group with a presentation $(s_0, \\dots, s_n | (s_is_j)^{m_{ij}} = e)$, where $m_{ij} \\in \\mathbb{Z}^+ \\cup \\{\\infty\\}$, with $m_{ii} = 1, m_{ji} = m_{ij} \\geq 2$ if $i \\neq j$, and $m_{ij} = \\infty$ means that there is no relation included for the pair $s_i, s_j$. Such a presentation is read off the Coxeter diagram of $(W,S)$ in a standard",
      "extractCut": true
    },
