      "extract": "Let $x \\mapsto \\overline{x}$ be the Kazhdan-Lusztig involution on $\\He(W,S)$. It is a $\\mathbb{Q}$-algebra involution, defined by the assignments $\\overline{v} = v^{-1}, \\overline{t_w} = t_{w^{-1}}^{-1}.$ Let $i:\\He(W,S)$ stand for the $\\mathcal{A}$-linear algebra anti-involution defined by $i(t_w) = t_{w^{-1}}$. For $h \\in \\He(W,S), x \\in W,$ let $h_x$ stand for the $t_x^{-1}$-coefficient of $h$ in the basis",
