      "extract": "\\label{sec:full-twist-jucys} Assume that $(W, S)$ is of finite type. Let $w_0$ stand for the longest element in $W$ with respect to the Bruhat length. Let $\\Se(W,S) = t_{w_0}^{-2} \\in \\He(W,S)$. In classical types, we will write $\\Se(X_n) \\in \\He(X_n)$, when $X$ is $A, B$ or $D$, or simply $\\Se$ when the type is clear from the context. The following proposition is also standard: \\begin{proposition}",
